{
  "requirement": "`habeas mdbook` MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters or captured-source\npages under the execution-coverage chapter of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index`. File-notes pages supporting coverage\ngap explanations under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes`\nMUST remain available.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test source only and did not request implementation source. `requirements.test-coverage.index.details` has two obligations. The first is that `habeas mdbook` MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters or captured-source pages under the coverage chapter. The second is that file-notes pages MUST remain available.\n\n**No per-test or captured-source pages.** `book_ignores_saved_measurements_and_preserves_artifacts` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It records a saved test attempt with `record(...)`, including a distinctive test name and profraw data. It then populates the book and asserts three things:\n- The chapter list is exactly `[\"Documented coverage gaps\", \"File notes: code.rs\"]`. A per-test subchapter or captured-source page would break this.\n- No chapter content contains the saved test name or `<select`.\n- No chapter path contains `-source`.\n\nIt repeats the check with invalid and empty `attempt.json`. It also asserts that the overview omits \"Captured source\", \"Test runs and provenance\", \"selected test attempts\" and \"Line coverage:\". This covers the negative obligation with recorded measurement data present, which is the case that could tempt a per-test page.\n\n**Hierarchy.** `generated_reports_inherit_the_requirements_index_hierarchy` is also marked `{test}`. It loops over every `coverage.sub_items` entry and asserts each has the expected parent names, section number and `../coverage.html` link, and no `source_path`. The check runs with both numbered and unnumbered parents. With the parent's `sub_items.len()` also asserted to be 2, nothing beyond coverage-page children appears.\n\n**File-notes pages remain available.** `documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups` is marked `{test}` for both this requirement and `index.file_map.notes`. For each documented file it finds the chapter named `File notes: {file}`. It asserts the chapter's path equals `notes::path(...)` and that its content contains `File: <code>{file}</code>` and the `coverage-note-N` anchors. It asserts the file card links to that page, and it asserts that exactly 5 `File notes:` chapters exist. `book_ignores_saved_measurements_and_preserves_artifacts` also shows `File notes: code.rs` still present beside a recorded attempt.\n\nBoth obligations have tests that exercise the behavior and assert its outcome. I found no gap.",
